aarch64: recognize three and four instruction constant sequences precisely
The four-instruction movptr form must coexist with the older three-instruction
forms used by narrow or legacy patch sites.  Identify MOVK words by their 64-bit
form, shift slot, and destination register instead of only checking the opcode.
Use the same predicate for patching and decoding, and return the actual number
of instructions so relocation callers invalidate the complete modified range.

Apply after 0020.  This corrects the previous conditional handling; it does not
change the four-instruction producer in 0019.

